      <title>Method</title>
      <sec id="s1a">
        <title>Participants</title>
        <p>We recruited 40 participants (see <xref ref-type="table" rid="t1">Table 1</xref>).<xref ref-type="fn" rid="fn1"><sup>1</sup></xref></p>
        <p>Materials are at <ext-link ext-link-type="doi" xlink:href="10.17605/OSF.IO/XYZ12">the project page</ext-link>.</p>
        <p>The code is on osf.io/qwert1 (see also www.example.org), e.g. for Fig.1.</p>
        <p>The posterior was <inline-formula><mml:math><mml:mrow><mml:mi>P</mml:mi><mml:mo>(</mml:mo><mml:mi>&#x3B2;</mml:mi><mml:mo>&gt;</mml:mo><mml:mn>0</mml:mn><mml:mo>)</mml:mo><mml:mo>=</mml:mo><mml:mn>.97</mml:mn><mml:mo>,</mml:mo><mml:mi>N</mml:mi><mml:mo>=</mml:mo><mml:mn>40</mml:mn></mml:mrow></mml:math></inline-formula>.</p>
      </sec>
    </sec>
    <sec id="s2">
      <title>Study 1</title>
      <sec id="s2a">
        <title>Results</title>
        <p>The effect was significant, <italic>t</italic>(38) = 2.50, <italic>p</italic> = .017, and the smallest <italic>p</italic> was 10<sup>&#x2212;5</sup> (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="r1 r2">Smith, 2020; Jones et al., 2019</xref>; <xref ref-type="fig" rid="f1">Figure 1</xref>).</p>
        <p>A range of citations [<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="r1">1</xref>&#x2013;<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="r3">3</xref>].</p>
        <list list-type="bullet">
